{
  "name": "wasp",
  "_about": "A wasp -- the common wasp (Vespula vulgaris), a worker 15 mm long: smooth, glossy and nearly hairless, in warning colours -- the gaster yellow, each ring with a black front band drawn back into a point on the midline and two black dots beside it; a pinched waist; the thorax black with yellow lines down its front edges and yellow spots on the scutellum; a yellow face with a black anchor mark, the eyes deeply notched; long black elbowed antennae; yellow legs; amber-smoked wings folded lengthwise at rest, lying narrow along the gaster's sides. Coat: the German wasp (three black dots on the face). Written whole by tools/creaturegen/rework/winged/hymen.py on insectlib.py + wlib.py (jointed legs on a walking gait, elbowed antennae that wave, the wings folded flat over the abdomen -- swung out and beating in the variant \"flying\").",
  "kind": "parts",
  "flags": {"print": "none", "legLen": 0.00525},
